{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1476406-vampires-as-reoccuring-villains","id":1476406,"title":"Vampires as reoccuring villains","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-03-14T18:11:49-07:00","id":1476406,"title":"Vampires as reoccuring villains","content":"I am planning a MtA campaign, which I hope to start in the late spring or early summer.<br /> <br /> The campaign will features a first awakening by the PC, and the arc will involve them dealing with the Traditions and the Technocracy. However, the main and re-occurring villains will be vampires. Specifically, Tremere who are getting up to shenanigans.<br /> <br /> I am posting here to ask for advice or suggestions on using vampires like this in a MtA game.<br /> <br /> What are your thoughts?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-14T19:16:37-07:00","id":1476410,"title":"","content":"Maybe read Blood Treachery? I\u2019ve never read it but I heard it\u2019s a good source on the conflict between the Tremere and the Order of Hermes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-14T19:41:51-07:00","id":1476413,"title":"","content":"Let's say you envision having five Tremere. Make three bad and two of them good or indispensable. One could be researching a magical problem(a curse works) that needs to be understood from a Thaumaturgical perspective, so that the Mentor or other helpful NPC says to hold back on hunting that particular Tremere until (s)he has finished the research and exchanged arcane data. Put the player in a position of having to earn the trust of that one Tremere researcher by avoiding hostility with the other four. In the local setting, establish a social fault line. Example, there is a violent gang in one part of town, maybe backed by the enemy Mage faction, the police tried to handle it with heavy handed tactics and are now reserved about doing anything further because of previous bad press. One of the Tremere occupies that social fault line and keeps the peace, at the cost of some actors' free will (Dominate). If that vampire were taken out, the city would be wracked violence.<br /> <br /> For the three really bad ones, they might use Dominate to frame a Technomancer for killing a group of sleepers with a hypertech weapon by altering the memories of witnesses. This creates a rogue Mage who the player's attention is focused on at the start. Their havens have to be well planned, so that the player can't just hit them during the day without careful investigation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":26467,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","user":"HorizonParty2021","date":". 03-27-2022, 09:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-15T09:17:53-07:00","id":1476437,"title":"","content":"There is a variable-level Thaumaturgical <i>Banning</i> ritual in one of the Dark Ages 20 books that I find indispensable to the orderly operation of practically any Mage chronicle in which an ST would like to position vampires as a credible threat to one or more mages. Notably, that ritual in Dark Ages 20 specifically name checks &quot;Pillars and Faiths&quot;, but that's just True Magick practiced under a an older, pre-Nine Spheres model, and there's no reason that modern Tremere wouldn't have developed a version that works for the Nine Spheres (assuming a new version is even necessary--again, it's all True Magick.)<br /> <br /> I won't get into the mechanics of the thing too much (because it's actually a series of rituals, <a href=\"https://saligia.fandom.com/wiki/Thaumaturgical_Rituals#Banning_Rituals\" target=\"_blank\">you can read more about it here</a>,) but suffice it to say that it puts the kibosh on the mages' attempt to use Correspondence to get around investigating, sleuthing, and dramatic conflict. The vampires put a symbol or mark of some kind on a door or building (i.e., a <i>place</i>) and it operates as a ban against not only willworkers but their magic(k)s as well--<b><i>not a ward</i></b> where you can just generate successes to overcome it, but a true and actual ban; no way around it other than to use correspondence of a higher rank than the level of the ritual (which goes at least as high as 5). Breaking the ban is actually very very easy, <i>but</i> you have to physically touch the thing... so the whole point here is not to make an impenetrable barrier, so much as to flummox remote viewing, searching, and smiting. That said performing the ritual is neither trivial nor easy, requires a decent amount of institutional support to perform (which should be fine for Tremere,) and the duration is measured in <u><i>weeks</i></u> per success. Adding to the logistical complications is the fact that banning Rank 2 (and lower) Spheres, and banning Rank 3 (and lower) Spheres, and so on, are different rituals that must each be learned separately (and there's a whole other set of rituals that do the same thing, but for vampire powers; and another set of rituals for shifter Gifts; and another set for Changeling powers; etc. etc. etc.) so there are probably dudes, or entire coteries, in the Tremere whose entire job is to know these rituals.<br /> <br /> In short, players don't get to Correspondence their way to easy street, but it's also a heavy-ish logistical lift for the Tremere to keep the thing going, particularly at higher levels. So if the mages are trying to dismantle a network of chantries in an area, there might be a low-level bullshit chantry annex somewhere they can Correspondence their way to relatively easily, either because it's not ritual'ed, or has a low-level version of the ritual that makes it findable by the mages--but they may never find the main/alpha site chantry in the city without an adept or master of Correspondence helping them. By that same token (and this is going to dovetail with HorizonParty2021's post above) you can get some spy/thriller vibes in there by setting up a situation where the mages find out (via investigation, interrogation, deduction, whatever,) who the banning specialist for the chantry or network of chantries is--this vampire now becomes and HVT, and you can get a few games in just trying to find, fix, and finish that one Tremere (and you know they're probably guarded by some heavy hitters too.) So, say they take the dude out, great, depending on when they last performed the banning ritual, there might still be weeks before the chantry has to worry about not being hidden; in the interim, they're probably going to have to take some tactical risks by breaking their typical patterns and exposing themselves as they find workarounds or bring someone new in. Enjoy your game of cat and also cat!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":2319,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","user":"CaptOtter","date":". 03-15-2022, 12:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-15T12:24:27-07:00","id":1476447,"title":"","content":"I\u2019d give some thought about what the general themes, vibes, and motifs you want the chronicle to have and extrapolate from their.<br /> <br /> More specifically, vampires are useful in that they\u2019ve got a lot of thematic flexibility. They\u2019ve been used as allegories for everything from pure evil to personal liberation, so you have a lot to potentially work with. I personally think that vampires as antagonists/monsters work best when used as a corruption, a cancer or parasite attached to humanity.<br /> <br /> Vampires infiltrate human societies and while some simply hunt within the crowd, a vampiric society will become an incestuous conspiracy of leeches. They\u2019ll seek to subvert every organization that could potentially interfere with their needs while seeking influence over anything that gives them power or can help them acquire blood. They use their gifts and skills to spread corruption, deceit, treachery, and the like because it makes the world more comfortable and ripe for them to exploit.<br /> <br /> Vampires are particularly nasty because not only do they have all the usual mundane methods of subversion but they also have supernatural means of spreading their corruption like a red virus. The kiss, the blood bond, presence, dominate, so on and so forth can all be used as tools to twist people into things which the vampires can better use.<br /> <br /> All of that applies to all vampires, including the Tremere. For the Tremere specifically though I\u2019d suggest thinking about what esoteric theories and ambitions they have. What great working are they planning to engage in and how can the characters and people they care about be pulled into the orbit of that occult project.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-15T18:20:03-07:00","id":1476482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CaptOtter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1476406-vampires-as-reoccuring-villains?p=1476437#post1476437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a variable-level Thaumaturgical <i>Banning</i> ritual in one of the Dark Ages 20 books that I find indispensable to the orderly operation of practically any Mage chronicle in which an ST would like to position vampires as a credible threat to one or more mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for this - I didn't know about this ritual. But I will look it up, and will probably use it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-01T00:23:38-07:00","id":1479869,"title":"","content":"A good consideration for Tremere is to determine what parts of Sleeper society they have infiltrated. Not just general things, like municipal services (firefighters, police, property inspectors, the IRS, blood banks, etc.), but specifically parts of society where the interests of Clan Tremere intersect with that of Mages.<br /> <br /> Academia, Occult enthusiast organizations, new age book stores. These places are often recruiting grounds for both Mages and Vampires.<br /> <br /> Any supply chains for &quot;esoteric materials&quot; would also qualify. It's not exactly simple to acquire the heart of murderer, or a branch taken from a tree struck by lightning, or a live owl, or a healthy bull with no blemishes. These kinds of specific (and sometimes illegal) materials are often only of interest to practicing magicians, and thus can be tricky and expensive to acquire, let alone expediently. They certainly exist, but you can't always acquire them on eBay (or be certain they're the real deal). Magicians benefit from networks of contacts who can not only acquire them, but do so reliably and discreetly. Because not only the magicians keep a lookout for them, but their enemies as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-01T07:44:58-07:00","id":1479894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1476406-vampires-as-reoccuring-villains?p=1479869#post1479869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A good consideration for Tremere is to determine what parts of Sleeper society they have infiltrated. Not just general things, like municipal services (firefighters, police, property inspectors, the IRS, blood banks, etc.), but specifically parts of society where the interests of Clan Tremere intersect with that of Mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>As an offshoot off the Order of Hermes, the Tremere are likely to deal in the same places and know that Mages thread there. In fact it wouldn't be a stretch for them to do so on purpose, keeping an eye open for Mage activity and maybe influencing it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-01T08:50:25-07:00","id":1479896,"title":"","content":"Some of these locations could just as easily be neutral ground for detente as they would be battlefields.<br /> <br /> Are the Hollow Ones' &quot;Outsider&quot; subgroup still a thing? Mages who gravitate toward the company of vampires for aesthetic reasons and even possibly serve as Blood Dolls could make for an interesting wild card. They could be romantic foils, Contacts or Allies on the inside, powerful antagonist henchmen, or the PC's themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11599,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","user":"Reasor","date":". 05-01-2022, 11:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-01T11:02:32-07:00","id":1479903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1476406-vampires-as-reoccuring-villains?p=1479896#post1479896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some of these locations could just as easily be neutral ground for detente as they would be battlefields.<br /> <br /> Are the Hollow Ones' &quot;Outsider&quot; subgroup still a thing? Mages who gravitate toward the company of vampires for aesthetic reasons and even possibly serve as Blood Dolls could make for an interesting wild card. They could be romantic foils, Contacts or Allies on the inside, powerful antagonist henchmen, or the PC's themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends on what the ST wants to do with the metaplot. They may or may not be tolerated by the Traditions. They may or may not be persecuted by them, for the actions of one of their members. They may or may not have thrown in with the Disparate Alliance.<br /> <br /> It does create plenty of interesting entanglements, to be sure. You might have a Hollow One blood doll that's trying to weasel their way into the good graces - and body of magical lore - of a Tremere Neonate. Or, conversely, a Tremere is dangling the possibility of revealing magical knowledge (probably lies) to a Hollow One is exchange for blood and favors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-02T18:35:26-07:00","id":1479996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1476406-vampires-as-reoccuring-villains?p=1479869#post1479869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any supply chains for &quot;esoteric materials&quot; would also qualify.</div> </div> </div> </div>The joke response is you can get anything on Amazon World of Darkness. The serious response is your post is good and I will have to determine how to use it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1208,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","user":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","date":". 05-02-2022, 09:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}